  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Located at 909 chemin de Font de Currault, on the edge of the Parc de la Valmasque, the Club Canin Mouginois offers dog training, agility and hoopers classes.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the City of Mougins' directory of sports associations (2021-2022 edition, the most recent found), dog training classes are held on Wednesdays and Saturdays at 3 pm, for dogs from 3 months old; an agility introduction follows on Saturdays, after the training classes. The club uses a positive natural method (reward with food or play), with a large share of socialisation between dogs and with people, and teaches owners the behaviours to adopt day to day. It is closed during the Christmas holidays, on public holidays and in July-August. Membership was then 220 € a year, from enrolment date to enrolment date.</p>
      <p>Check before you go: these times and this price date from 2021-2022 and were not found on a recent club page. The domain clubcaninmouginois.fr, given at the time, no longer leads to the club (it now shows a gambling site): do not enter any information there and go through the Mougins town hall (04 92 92 50 00) to reach the club. The club was still active in October 2024: it gave an obedience demonstration at the "L'animal, moi &amp; Cie" day organised by the city of Mougins at the Eco'Parc (programme on mougins.fr).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the Parc de la Valmasque right next door lets you extend the outing with a walk in the forest.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Parc de la Valmasque, with its riding centre and trails, is directly accessible from the club.</p>
